ption":"Dendrochronology","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7f8f-8f73-63fa70eeb787","description":"Magnetic dating","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-78cb-a0e9-86c20f768bab","description":"Thermoluminescence","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-723f-a059-c18df519e014","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the term for the cleaning process that birds engage in?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Many birds spread oil from a gland near the tail over their feathers during preening, helping maintain their plumage.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7961-9b10-2ed7abc88c39","description":"Preening","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7242-8b7b-36bb46c84c6e","description":"Sweening","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7d3d-b3ee-1d78d9c3577f","description":"Greening","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-77a5-b92c-6e2cb7a366f6","description":"Feening","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-70c7-b48c-3264a1536e30","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the sum of 1+2+3+4+5?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The sum is 15: the pairs 1+5 and 2+4 each total 6, and adding the middle term, 3, gives the result.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-371e-77cc-9a60-34a8cab2b835","description":"15","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7036-bc10-b82f64f2b95b","description":"9","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-71c9-b47d-790439aa0657","description":"10","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-792d-95e0-40bac2b14357","description":"14","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-78fb-9bc3-d134ef475d76","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Rhinology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Rhinology studies the nose and its diseases. The name combines a Greek root for the nose with -logy, meaning study.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7e30-91ef-91e6c1e090c6","description":"the nose and its diseases","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7570-b461-54efff97ee61","description":"ants","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7826-8e65-4d4a70cfb98b","description":"origin of life","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7ca2-892a-4e8b6888cd05","description":"the age of trees and the records in their rings","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7fde-8e23-1f24be6a460d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What are the 2 parts of complex numbers known as?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"In a + bi, a is the real part, while b is the coefficient of the imaginary unit i.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-371e-79bd-947c-9c543e8c83ff","description":"Real & Imaginary","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-71b5-8a57-07f5297aebe0","description":"True & False","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-79e3-bc04-e510c6dea059","description":"Big & Small","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-700e-bf3a-d0a1a9c1dd63","description":"Logical & Intuitive","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-371e-7756-b617-29eba649d0b6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which Soviet spacecraft carried the dog Laika into orbit in 1957?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Laika became the first animal to orbit Earth aboard Sputnik 2, but she did not return alive.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7eb5-b65b-58d38b7988ef","description":"Sputnik 2","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7d36-8344-7382dd1b1e76","description":"Sputnik 1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-70bf-ac4b-0308956b9c6d","description":"Vostok 1","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7da7-8f99-268fdac255ff","description":"Luna 2","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7f47-a795-e335f36c62a3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the smallest bird in the world?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Bee Hummingbird is native to Cuba, and females are slightly larger than males.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-371f-72a9-a825-10b462dcad6c","description":"Bee Hummingbird","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7a64-a39b-690d59ca67f2","description":"Pigeon","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-78fb-b352-2acaa5fba1a6","description":"Great Horned Owl","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7769-82ee-2030f5a70445","description":"Ostrich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7e8d-b317-606d2057be33","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What infectious lung disease is known by two letters?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"TB stands for tuberculosis, a bacterial infection that most often affects the lungs and can spread through the air.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7eea-8226-afef10b93d58","description":"TB","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-741e-bbde-a2e8657c55d4","description":"HF","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-762d-923d-011d578903af","description":"CC","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7b62-a91e-0e66da026dd1","description":"AK","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-76f8-8707-5d88f7d5edaf","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Venereology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Venereology is the study of sexually transmitted diseases. Its name is related to \u201cvenereal,\u201d a term historically associated with Venus, the Roman goddess of love.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7866-a11a-2f51bc6090f1","description":"Sexually transmitted diseases","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7aa5-b229-e806cf1565f2","description":"Vocal sounds","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-7b97-90b6-a28a0f86a269","description":"Grasshoppers and crickets","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-371f-70a1-bc2d-396061bab308","description":"Ants","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f