ight angles, each measuring 90\u00b0, so their sum is 360\u00b0.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-768b-ab81-a14df9ae00dd","description":"360\u00b0","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-73e1-b13b-ec2c707cd582","description":"480\u00b0","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-70f9-98cf-1a6d5e252b71","description":"90\u00b0","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-78fd-8989-74d91c7dfeb9","description":"180\u00b0","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7101-82fb-b5512ce6199d","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What was Colossus, the machine used at Bletchley Park during World War II?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Colossus was a code-breaking computer that analyzed Lorenz-encrypted German teleprinter messages using thousands of vacuum tubes.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-726c-87fd-485b206a7d70","description":"A code-breaking computer","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7931-aeb1-a6a70bf296a3","description":"A nuclear-resistant tank","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7ec8-a8b7-630608b59c3a","description":"A supersonic bomber","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7ca0-88ba-493225b008ca","description":"An intercontinental missile","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7cde-9460-27247eb46161","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Ecophysiology the study of?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ecophysiology links physiology with ecology, examining how conditions such as drought affect a plant\u2019s water use and growth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-721e-9997-d8406740919c","description":"How the environment interacts with an organism","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-71c6-972a-ce0de88708d2","description":"The art of bell ringing","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7f42-b5ae-ab6e2ea160d9","description":"Bats","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7523-bad4-6c0be0e6c56d","descript