atives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-70e8-a492-a1ac35ca011a","description":"A gaggle","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7860-ba74-8e333049fbc0","description":"A nest","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-755f-9a8f-cf9c09bfda4f","description":"A pride","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7d51-ad71-fc96efc49b8f","description":"A gang","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-73c1-9f74-62c59b06b0a3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which planet is known for having the Great Red Spot?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Jupiter\u2019s Great Red Spot is a giant storm in its atmosphere that has been observed for centuries.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-70be-a03e-969bbd8439cf","description":"Jupiter","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-733b-813c-f995001ca8d6","description":"Saturn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7747-ba2c-56a086861b17","description":"Mars","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7ec3-9ba9-43e31a8e48c7","description":"Neptune","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7071-a3b7-e0f9f1511208","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Who discovered the structure of the atom?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ernest Rutherford inferred the atom\'s compact, positively charged nucleus after some alpha particles bounced sharply off thin gold foil.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-75cc-a380-ce76b7292169","description":"Ernest Rutherford","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7cc1-8115-d0679c6eeea3","description":"Albert Einstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7987-8a7f-3a6bf576de96","description":"J. J. Thomson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-71ab-a567-e3ca657fb8f7","description":"Niels Bohr","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7d5f-87b4-429a5c9cc740","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name for a hot spring that shoots 