":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-796b-b9ab-6df23943a1db","description":"The spread of diseases","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7554-8049-7e4a5e48fd8f","description":"Rocks","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7485-b082-44b85aa556c5","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the bending of light when it enters a different medium?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Refraction happens because light changes speed as it passes between materials, such as air and water, changing its direction.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-788e-9d8d-69f6523a08be","description":"Refraction","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7f97-9cd0-4d512f43bd29","description":"Reflection","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-740d-92b0-50ac8718f13f","description":"Convection","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7b51-9a38-2803dcb97a07","description":"Ablation","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7621-9b3a-fac6631318a5","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which substance takes its name from the Greek for `not flammable\'?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Asbestos fibers were used in insulation and other heat-resistant materials, but inhaling them can cause serious disease.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7db4-8366-bcb08d3d64d6","description":"Asbestos","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7d23-8ad2-689c4193ce73","description":"Bleach","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-797b-89c0-06ca22a2ecff","description":"Ethanol","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7317-889a-34d322f9816c","description":"Methadone","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7dc1-9c6f-0a75eccdbef2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In mammals, which organ produces milk?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Mammary glands are modified sweat glands, and prolactin helps stimulate milk production after birth.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-775c-9acb-801ad7a58d89","description":"Mammary gland","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7f89-ac43-29517e4452e8","description":"Prostate","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-793b-8e62-c7375c985bc4","description":"Pancreas","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7474-a406-3bcd2470dba4","description":"Pituitary gland","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7910-8614-7a1501ee5807","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which organisms use gills for breathing?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Many aquatic mollusks, including clams and squid, breathe through gills, while some land-dwelling members breathe with lungs.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7383-9acd-3981739cbb02","description":"Mollusks","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-732c-9c0b-a75c8d355ee5","description":"Penguins","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7d65-9330-db221fbc2c00","description":"Bacteria","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7a01-91b7-deadf281690e","description":"Mangroves","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7073-9687-b432a4fa81c9","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which system of counting uses the numbers 0-9 and the letters a-f?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Hexadecimal is base 16; computer color codes commonly use it, with values such as #FFFFFF representing white.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7108-afeb-847c3a8e286a","description":"Hexadecimal","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7514-934e-5575924790e9","description":"Numerolettering","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7960-b317-f5d28ab27fcd","description":"Binary","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7fe8-85d6-db31d5a1d6c8","description":"Ternary","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-730d-a0f7-19dae436d6dc","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"A male chicken is known as what?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Roosters are known for their loud crowing call, which often signals the start of the day.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-748b-826a-e54cba72e718","description":"A Rooster","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-73e7-ab97-98d1a2829570","description":"A Buck","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-79c6-8d51-12d2d5e18a99","description":"A Dog","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-73ee-ae47-07f773b5d919","description":"A Ram","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-70db-bd4d-9cbeb835b02f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What procedure involved cutting the connections to and from the prefrontal cortex of the brain?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Lobotomy\u2019s developer, Ant\u00f3nio Egas Moniz, received the 1949 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine for work on the therapeutic value of leucotomy.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7739-a0ef-1e185a4069eb","description":"Lobotomy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7a48-83a4-fe74040abd18","description":"Electroconvulsive therapy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7147-a9ca-a15f50362a80","description":"Insulin shock therapy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7823-8a90-a60af8a43953","description":"Trepanning","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-76fc-a0e9-7aab5efacecb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the physical law that states that energy is neither created or destroyed?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Law of Conservation of Energy says energy can change forms but the total remains constant in an isolated system.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-75bf-9658-1305706077e1","description":"Law of Conservation of Energy","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7586-af6b-5b761a2e00fe","description":"Law of Universal Gravitation","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-710f-9e54-f47100d0ab2b","description":"Law of Thermodynamics","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7a38-9a45-48925353bd21","description":"Law of the Lever","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7054-bf8d-41fb8517516c","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the streak of light called when a space rock burns up as it enters Earth\'s atmosphere?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"A meteor is the streak of light, often called a shooting star, made when a meteoroid burns up in the atmosphere.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7c3b-b86c-46d70fa92240","description":"Meteor","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-703d-892e-4406659b617b","description":"Comet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-746c-9615-00710807ddaf","description":"Pulsar","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-754f-a3bd-0aca14fea74f","description":"Aurora","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-785b-939f-6ea9dabed8e3","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the study of human beings and their cultures?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Anthropology is often divided into cultural, biological, linguistic, and archaeological branches, which study humans from different perspectives.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-76b5-a001-4a693e17f5c9","description":"Anthropology","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7256-91a0-0eb257f9dce9","description":"Anthology","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7013-8263-3565142f411d","description":"Geography","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-75d3-a9f4-7b74333cdf73","description":"Apiology","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-748b-8448-1a57550fc179","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the soil that is always frozen and helps to define the boundary of the Arctic?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Permafrost is ground that remains at or below freezing for at least two consecutive years; a seasonally thawed active layer can sit above it.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7274-b702-386255a13921","description":"Permafrost","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7bb8-9967-e8b0add2d89d","description":"Icerock","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-770b-bf85-6ae795739bb5","description":"Coolground","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7991-a788-7bad5dc9eeef","description":"Evercold","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-70dc-9d4f-d3e7edba4b42","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which of these is a popular programming language?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Java was developed at Sun Microsystems and became widely known for running on many kinds of computers.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7762-be7f-92d3463f945a","description":"Java","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7218-9496-dcea3ee8c470","description":"Flark","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7388-972b-37dca0bac62a","description":"Goku","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7f77-82f0-fb7590cedaca","description":"Anon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7f78-bb45-5af1b0c6bb92","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In which region of the solar system does the dwarf planet Pluto orbit?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Kuiper Belt is a ring-shaped region beyond Neptune that contains many icy bodies, including Pluto.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-74ff-aeb9-5497852031a8","description":"The Kuiper Belt","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7ee4-bf54-c6354e8aae87","description":"The Oort Cloud","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-777f-a308-96d94cd5cebd","description":"The Asteroid Belt","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7659-925b-6cd93f812c92","description":"The Scattered Disc","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7368-b621-17876b0da14f","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-1