,"alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7bcf-bd0c-2e777baf3dba","description":"Virtual reality","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-736d-af2b-7fa020cc22d8","description":"Augmented reality","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7d92-ab66-6c9af32e0fa5","description":"Mixed media","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7181-9fa4-5f1eb4f05f4e","description":"Digital hologram","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7e63-a8bf-42eee90c47bb","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which dwarf planet is the only one located in the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Ceres was discovered by Giuseppe Piazzi in 1801 and was initially classified as a planet before later being designated a dwarf planet.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7dd3-b3d6-849e41c0a698","description":"Ceres","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7349-bee3-f0bdf4a64ab1","description":"Eris","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-76da-ac2c-ea2e1fc0982e","description":"Haumea","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-719d-bddb-727a4696c652","description":"Vesta","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7de7-bb85-eff6974e1bb2","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Dinosaur names have two parts, the first being the genus. What does the second part denote?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The second part of a binomial name, such as rex in Tyrannosaurus rex, is the species name.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7c38-bd21-7ac4ed166e9b","description":"The species","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7493-9ff5-3cad785317a3","description":"The habitat","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-757c-8e0c-31260367de56","description":"The size","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-78e6-b3a8-d53dc4658c4a","description":"The discoverer","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-76eb-af06-884cbe9aea50","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"In an attempt to finance German WWI reparations, which chemist tried to extract gold from seawater?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Fritz Haber investigated recovering gold from seawater, but the concentration was too low for the process to be practical.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7a4b-bc10-0dda26393930","description":"Fritz Haber","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7050-a51e-d8b20d270eec","description":"Marie Curie","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-784d-805d-4ec98f277c88","description":"Albert Einstein","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-741d-862e-72ff8d4ba8c9","description":"Robert Boyle","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-787b-87c1-f9d4bf19bb12","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"By what means are the gases of the atmosphere held close to Earth?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Gravity pulls atmospheric particles toward Earth, preventing most from drifting into space; the same force governs planetary orbits.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-741d-a283-19647367a9e3","description":"Gravity","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7be4-b6e7-6501aac07ab5","description":"Friction","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-749f-9113-c97158634eba","description":"Coriolis Force","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7c08-acd6-648419768699","description":"Ground effect","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7e90-acb9-e8d54fb8c558","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of the closest large spiral galaxy to our galaxy?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"The Andromeda Galaxy is moving toward the Milky Way and is expected to merge with it in the distant future.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7068-96a6-fd47787bf00b","description":"Andromeda","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7991-8758-9f27444a5732","description":"Hercules","correct_answe