a began breaking apart as tectonic plates shifted, eventually separating into the continents we know today.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-770e-9b87-a3661a57ada0","description":"Pangaea","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7e95-b284-f471288ce842","description":"Laurasia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7b73-880c-09918544ae57","description":"Rodinia","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7055-bd0c-a14eb07e4644","description":"Gondwana","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-725c-944b-a1ffbb47d6e6","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name given to a poison that acts on the nervous system?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Neurotoxins affect nerve cells or their signaling. Botulinum toxin is one example; it disrupts communication between nerves and muscles.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7e6a-a368-8a56242c905e","description":"Neurotoxins","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-72de-a0b3-81be00d4c47d","description":"Neurovenoms","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3720-7399-a411-364755d81534","description":"Endotoxins","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3721-741c-91eb-074d73444e21","description":"Endovenoms","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3721-7d43-ad4d-25f3952ca0c4","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which particles are emitted by cathode ray tubes?","difficulty":2,"explanation":"Cathode rays are streams of electrons; J. J. Thomson\u2019s studies of them helped establish that atoms contain these particles.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3721-703c-850b-65d11361fa56","description":"Electrons","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3721-7ade-9bf6-994d07bd1340","description":"Ions","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3721-7357-b33a-321ec1b01287","description":"Neutrons","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3721-709c-8772-a2fdedebaeb6","description":"Bosons","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218